# QRP reconstruction

## Read first (in git)

1. `docs/product/QRP_RECONSTRUCTION_SPIRIT.md` — mission, Phase 1–2 split, local-only rules
2. `docs/product/QRP_API_IMPLEMENTATION_MATRIX.md` — route/API status (code truth)
3. `docs/product/QRP_UI_RECONSTRUCTION_PLAN.md` — dependency order; no mass reskin
4. `docs/product/QRP_END_TO_END_WORKFLOW.md` — lifecycle; separate approval stages
5. `docs/product/FULL_STACK_STATUS.md` + `WORKSPACE_UI_CATALOG.md` + `QRP_DESIGN_SYSTEM.md`

## Local only — do not add or commit

- `vendor-references/**`
- `docs/reference-analysis/**`
- `docs/research/VENDOR_REFERENCE_UI.md`

Use those paths on disk for research if present. Progress notes belong in a **local** `docs/reference-analysis/IMPLEMENTATION_LOG.md` or commit message — not new tracked research trees.

## Hard rules

| Do | Do not |
| --- | --- |
| Vertical slice: API + migration + tests + `FULL_STACK_STATUS` | Cosmetic pass without backend |
| `require_permission` + scoped checks in services | Unguarded routes |
| Honest empty/error states | Fake KPIs or demo counts in production paths |
| Pattern-only from AGPL/GPL vendors | Vendor code in product tree |
| Contextual workflow on detail/wizard | Global governance rail on list hubs |

## Commits

Product changes only: code, migrations, tests, `docs/product/*` (spirit, status, catalog, design). **Never** commit vendor clone analysis markdown.